                <pb facs="0114" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg2"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.71 Manchuria/77: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-01-04T18:00:00-05:00">January 4, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. Your 1, January 1, noon.</p>
                <p>If and when ordinary mail service between China and Manchukuo is begun and parcel
                    post and money order services are inaugurated, please report by radio.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
